WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:11.682
Hi! One cat is a cat, and two are two cats. But why do we say an egg? Today we'll learn singular and plural nouns, and a and an.

2
00:00:11.832 --> 00:00:16.314
Before a consonant sound, use a: a cat, a ball.

3
00:00:16.464 --> 00:00:22.602
Before a vowel sound, a, e, i, o or u, use an: an egg, an apple.

4
00:00:22.752 --> 00:00:26.706
An umbrella, an ant: both start with a vowel.

5
00:00:26.856 --> 00:00:31.074
We use a and an only for one thing.

6
00:00:31.224 --> 00:00:34.770
Most nouns just add s: cats, books.

7
00:00:34.920 --> 00:00:42.954
Nouns ending in s, x, sh or ch add es: buses, boxes, dishes, watches.

8
00:00:43.104 --> 00:00:49.098
If a noun ends in a consonant and y, change y to i and add es: babies.

9
00:00:49.248 --> 00:00:56.106
Some nouns change in special ways: men, children, feet, teeth.

10
00:00:56.256 --> 00:01:00.978
Watch out! Elephant starts with e, so we can't use a!

11
00:01:01.128 --> 00:01:03.834
Before a vowel sound, use an.

12
00:01:03.984 --> 00:01:07.506
So it's an elephant.

13
00:01:07.656 --> 00:01:17.130
Your turn! I ate, ___, orange. A or an? Pause and think.

14
00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:22.578
Orange starts with o, so an. Did you get it right?

15
00:01:22.728 --> 00:01:32.442
Another one! She has, ___, red bag. A or an? Pause and think.

16
00:01:32.592 --> 00:01:38.514
Red starts with the consonant r, so a. Did you get it right?

17
00:01:38.664 --> 00:01:47.466
Here's another! There are three, ___. Which one? Pause and think.

18
00:01:47.616 --> 00:01:54.450
Box ends in x, so add es: boxes. Did you get it right?

19
00:01:54.600 --> 00:02:03.690
Try one more! Two, ___, are crying. Which one? Pause and think.

20
00:02:03.840 --> 00:02:10.290
Change y to i and add es: babies. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:10.440 --> 00:02:19.362
Try one more! I have ten, ___. Which one? Pause and think.

22
00:02:19.512 --> 00:02:25.290
Ten means more than one, so toes. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:34.626
Try one more! Many, ___, are playing. Which one? Pause and think.

24
00:02:34.776 --> 00:02:40.170
The plural of child is children. Did you get it right?

25
00:02:40.320 --> 00:02:49.746
Last one! He wants, ___, umbrella. A or an? Pause and think.

26
00:02:49.896 --> 00:02:55.434
Umbrella starts with u, so an. Did you get it right?

27
00:02:55.584 --> 00:03:07.890
Remember: a before a consonant, an before a vowel. Plurals usually add s; s, x, sh and ch add es; consonant plus y becomes ies.

28
00:03:08.040 --> 00:03:12.642
Count things at home and say them in English!

